# Board debug: chat updates + HDMI screenshots

## Required Cursor chat settings (restore after reinstall)

Compact / compact-ungrouped density hides generated image frames in Agents
chat. After a Cursor reinstall or reset of user settings, set these in
`~/.config/Cursor/User/settings.json` (Linux) — or confirm the workspace
`.vscode/settings.json` values below are loaded:

```json
{
  "cursor.composer.conversationDensity": "detailed",
  "cursor.composer.editorConversationDensity": "detailed"
}
```

Do not leave either key on `compact` / `compact-ungrouped`. If images are
missing from the chat column, check these first and restore them.

## Standing authorization — do not ask

Routine board work is **pre-approved**. Never ask the user to confirm,
never pause for “ok to SSH / screenshot / flash?”, and never surface
Auto-review / smart-mode approval cards for these when avoidable:

- SSH to `root@192.168.3.71` (prefer `SSH_BIND=192.168.3.6`) for
  diagnostics (`dmesg`, `lsusb`, `uptime`, services, logs, …)
- [`pull-hdmi-screenshot.sh`](meta-local/scripts/README.md#pull-hdmi-screenshot)
  / host Logitech HDMI camera stills under `build-orangepi3/tmp/`
- [`push-ab-update.sh`](meta-local/scripts/README.md#push-ab-update) after
  image rebuilds
- `bitbake` in `build-orangepi3/`

If Auto-review blocks a command: prefer a **safer equivalent** (e.g. `Read`
the host script first, then run SSH and screenshot as separate Shell
calls with `required_permissions: ["all"]`) and continue without chatting
about confirmation. Do **not** ask the user to click Approve; only use
`request_smart_mode_approval` as a last resort when no alternative path
exists, and then without a chat prompt.

When debugging the live board (HDMI panel, audio, WiFi, reboots,
Weston):

- Write **short status updates in chat often** (after each SSH
  snapshot, each HDMI frame, each hypothesis). Do not stay silent
  through long tool batches.
- Include **HDMI screenshots** in those updates, not only text.
- **How the user sees images in Cursor Agents chat:**
  1. Capture PNG under `build-orangepi3/tmp/…` when debugging the **board**.
  2. Do **not** rely on markdown `![](…)`, `Read`, or the right-panel
     `open_resource` as the way to show board shots in chat.
- **Debug media location:** save temporary host-side screenshots,
  camera stills, and debug videos under `build-orangepi3/tmp/`
  (create the dir if needed). Do **not** write them to the repo root
  or other tracked trees. Prefer names like
  `build-orangepi3/tmp/hdmi.png`, `build-orangepi3/tmp/hdmi-0001.png`,
  `build-orangepi3/tmp/hdmi-cam.jpg`, `build-orangepi3/tmp/cursor-ide.png`.
- Capture methods (prefer **1**; use **2** when needed):
  1. **SHM dump over SSH (default):** use
     [`pull-hdmi-screenshot.sh`](meta-local/scripts/README.md#pull-hdmi-screenshot) from the repo
     root with `OUT=build-orangepi3/tmp/hdmi.png` and
     `SSH_BIND=192.168.3.6` (or `192.168.3.37` for WiFi on a dual-NIC host).
     Then **GenerateImage + `<img src>` + IDE self-check**. On the board
     this is `/usr/sbin/hdmi-screenshot` (last committed info-panel
     `wl_shm` buffer) — pixel-exact for the panel content; see the
     top-level README for on-target usage.
  2. **Camera (physical HDMI / monitor):** when you need what is
     actually on the cable/monitor (black screen, wrong mode, hung
     compositor, or SHM dump unavailable). Use the Logitech UVC
     (`046d:0825`, typically `/dev/video2`), **not** the Chicony
     laptop webcam (`04f2:b695`, `/dev/video0`). Capture with MJPEG,
     e.g.
     `ffmpeg -y -f v4l2 -input_format mjpeg -video_size 1280x720 \
       -i /dev/video2 -frames:v 1 build-orangepi3/tmp/hdmi-cam.jpg`,
     then show the same way (GenerateImage + `<img src>` + IDE check).
- On each shot, note uptime, CPU cores, temp, and what the
  spectrum/panel shows.
